Package: wintogo
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends},
         python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, python3-hivex,
         wimtools, ntfs-3g, gdisk, dosfstools, mtools, 7zip | p7zip-full,
         pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: qemu-utils
Suggests: qemu-system-x86, ovmf
Description: install Windows To Go onto a USB drive from Linux
 Applies a Windows 10 or 11 edition from an ISO onto a USB drive (or a
 disk image file) so that it boots on any UEFI PC, Secure Boot included,
 without a Windows machine or VM. It partitions the drive, applies the
 image with wimlib, edits the offline registry and answer file for
 first-time setup, and writes the boot files and BCD store itself.
 .
 Windows can also be installed into a VHDX file on the drive and booted
 from there (needs qemu-utils). wintogo-vm boots a drive or image in QEMU
 for testing (needs qemu-system-x86 and ovmf).
